Cell["\<\
The tree is the contraction schedule: the leaves are the circuit's gate and \
state tensors, every internal node is one pairwise contraction, and the \
branching structure is the order the greedy path chose, showing which \
contractions are nested. The depth and balance of that tree are what the path \
adjusts to keep each intermediate tensor small.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"53291d47-a111-bd44-02d6-9520d0a507ae"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The stabilizer engine: the state as its symmetry group", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"14460f59-6b0f-818e-3c7d-a7030ebbd3d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For Clifford circuits there is a representation that does not use \
amplitudes: store the state as the group of Pauli operators that fix it, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["P", "TI"], ":", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
       "Ket"]}]}], "=", 
    RowBox[{"+", 
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
      "Ket"]}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6afe19ed-5a5e-331e-1a85-90b75fe89e64"],
 ", whose ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "142f588d-e120-bc70-3dd5-51d690da075a"],
 " commuting generators determine the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "029948d8-232c-2201-32a7-618256d9716b"],
 "-qubit state uniquely and fit in a binary symplectic tableau. This is the \
Gottesman-Knill representation, in which a Clifford gate is a constant-size \
rewrite of the tableau rather than a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[Times]", 
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b1b5b6f-b43d-594b-7939-53493dc82b91"],
 " matrix product. The engine is selected by one option. Build a five-qubit \
linear cluster state, the entangled resource behind measurement-based \
computing, as a layer of Hadamards followed by nearest-neighbor controlled-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "32f703b9-71e1-95eb-628c-9ae30795ff31"],
 " gates:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c860bbc-8d1f-f590-34bd-a2e624abdffa"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"cluster5", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", "5", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<CZ\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[64]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1bab88a0-6539-d521-49a8-210a0ccdbc0b"],

